WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:06.580
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and since the
back half of this season on The Flash is going

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:10.210
to be littered with Rogues, I wanted to do
a bonus video explaining the ones they’re

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.210
doing.

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:14.320
Or at least the ones they’ve announced so
far.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.320
And a few they might still add.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.860
They just cast Peyton List as Lisa Snart aka
Golden Glider.

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:20.310
She’s Captain Cold’s sister.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:22.340
I’m sure Robbie Amell was pumped to hear
that.

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:26.490
Now they can add The Tomorrow People to the
list of shows they’re snagging people from.

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:28.760
Prison Break, Spartacus and now Tomorrow People.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:33.470
She won’t appear till Episode 16, but Episode
17, the one right after that, will feature

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:38.100
Mark Hamill reprising his Trickster character
from the original Flash series.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:45.040
This video will mostly be about Heatwave because
he’s in the promo for the next episode and

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:47.430
all the new Rogues they’ve already announced.

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:48.540
So who are the Rogues?

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:53.620
If you haven’t read the comics, they’re
a revolving cast of misfits with B-Level abilities

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:56.909
that act as a crime gang in both Central City
and Keystone City.

00:00:56.909 --> 00:01:01.410
The size of their gang changes from comic
to comic, but there are always a couple of

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:07.120
core members that stay the same.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:15.490
The oldest ones from the classic comics are
Captain Cold, Heatwave, Weather Wizard, Trickster,

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:22.830
Mirror Master, Pied Piper, Golden Glider,
Abra Kadabra and The Top.

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:26.000
Most of those people are already on the show.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:36.130
In the early 2000s they introduced Double
Down, Tar Pit, Plunder, Girder and Murmur

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:41.360
The New 52 version of the rogues if very close
to the classic version.

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:45.100
But there have also been alternate groups,
like the Renegades, which are a future version

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:56.280
of their group from the 25th Century, but
the twist is that their like a police task

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:57.280
force.

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:03.159
And during Final Crisis, Inertia creates this
splinter group called the New Rogues as a

00:02:03.159 --> 00:02:08.979
way to piss the original Rogues off and blackmail
them into working for him.

00:02:08.979 --> 00:02:12.500
Since the TV Show is still in season 1 they’re
mostly sticking with the classic versions

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:13.610
of the characters.

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:17.560
Anytime you’re looking for Rogue easter
eggs in their episodes mostly be looking for

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:24.030
stuff from the original versions of the characters
all the way through Geoff Johns Run pre-Flashpoint.

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:28.560
So far they’ve introduced Weather Wizard
in episode 1, Captain Cold and Heatwave in

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:32.860
Episode 4, the post credits scene from that
is where Captain Cold actually forms the Rogues

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:39.870
officially when he says “I’m forming a
new team”.

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:44.920
Girder debuted in Episode 6, as far as we
know he died in Episode 7 helping them fight

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:45.920
Blackout.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:46.920
He only appears in the comics during Flashpoint
so I don’t consider Blackout a Rogue.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:57.270
Captain Boomerang is only mentioned in the
Flash vs Arrow Crossover episode.

00:02:57.270 --> 00:02:59.220
And then the Reverse Flash finally appeared
in Episode 9.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:03.380
He’s technically not a rogue, but a lot
of his stories in the comics get tied up with

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:04.380
the Rogues.

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:08.051
He either uses them or they cross paths because
they’re both trying to take out one of the

00:03:08.051 --> 00:03:11.430
Flashes, Barry Allen, Wally West or Bart Allen.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:15.440
So don’t be surprised if by the end of Season
1 or in the finale.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:19.300
They Rogues and The Reverse Flash appear on
screen together.

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:23.220
As far as we know Captain Cold’s gun is
the most effective weapon against him.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:27.130
And now based on their fight in episode 9,
we know Firestorm’s powers work really well

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:28.130
against him.

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:34.180
I guess I should also say that on very rare
occasions, Captain Cold has worked with The

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:36.000
Flash, when it’s suited him.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:38.400
He might be a criminal, but he does live by
a code.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.720
I already did a video for Captain Cold so
I’ll add a link in the description if you

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:51.569
want to watch it after this but at the time
they had not cast his sister.

00:03:51.569 --> 00:03:54.500
Lisa Snart or Golden Glider.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.910
That’s Peyton List.

00:03:56.910 --> 00:04:00.560
He turned to a life of crime to support his
sister, they came from an abusive household,

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:05.050
so when they both took off, he took it on
himself to support her, keep her safe.

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:06.970
That’s why he became a bank robber.

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:11.400
After he got the cold gun things got a little
crazy, but you get the idea.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:16.269
He’s not out to get the flash, all he cares
about is his sister.

00:04:16.269 --> 00:04:20.559
Robbing people and mercenary work are the
only options he sees.

00:04:20.559 --> 00:04:23.830
So meeting Peyton List on the show is going
to be a lot of fun.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:28.180
In the comics, she became a Rogue in her own
right, and in the new 52 she even got her

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:29.180
own special powers.

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:32.949
But since the show is going with the classic
versions, if she does end up committing any

00:04:32.949 --> 00:04:33.949
crimes.

00:04:33.949 --> 00:04:38.719
She’ll probably look a little more like
a Cat Burglar.

00:04:38.719 --> 00:04:41.889
The dynamic between her and Wenworth Miller
is going to be so much fun.

00:04:41.889 --> 00:04:46.419
She’s like the voice of reason out of that
whole bunch.

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:51.419
Heatwave, who’s being played by fellow Prison
Break Alum Dominic Purcell is the flipside

00:04:51.419 --> 00:04:52.419
of that.

00:04:52.419 --> 00:04:55.629
He’s not related to Captain Cold, but they’ve
been friends for most of their adult lives.

00:04:55.629 --> 00:04:59.960
Heatwave, as the name implies is a powder
keg of ego waiting to explode.

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:04.979
He’s got an ichy trigger finger and he’s
not very bright and he causes a lot of collateral

00:05:04.979 --> 00:05:06.860
damage for the rogues.

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:09.330
He and Captain Cold butt heads in the comics
a lot.

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:10.330
Song of Ice and Fire.

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:12.030
It’s right out of Game of Thrones.

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:15.610
The show kind of teased that in episode 4
in that post credits scene where Wentworth

00:05:15.610 --> 00:05:18.930
Miller is like “i know that last job didn’t
go so well…”

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:22.169
As far as we know, they’ll be the only two
Rogues in episode 10.

00:05:22.169 --> 00:05:26.949
But it’s called Revenge of the Rogues, which
is a reference to the comic book storyline

00:05:26.949 --> 00:05:28.530
“Rogues Revenge”.

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:33.159
I think it’s a reference in name only, because
Rogues Revenge was from Final Crisis and it

00:05:33.159 --> 00:05:37.689
involved Bart Allen and Inertia and a lot
of characters we don’t have on the show

00:05:37.689 --> 00:05:38.689
yet.

00:05:38.689 --> 00:05:42.930
So this is mostly going to be the Rogues first
mission as a team.

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:45.699
With Caitlin being used as blackmail.

00:05:45.699 --> 00:05:49.249
They’re probably after Star LABS tech or
they want The Flash to steal something for

00:05:49.249 --> 00:05:50.249
them.

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:51.249
It’s going to be a lot of fun.

00:05:51.249 --> 00:05:53.610
Expect Dominic Purcell to go completely crazy.

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:57.340
The next new Rogue we’ll meet is Pied Piper.

00:05:57.340 --> 00:06:04.339
He’s actually in two episodes 11 and 12.

00:06:04.339 --> 00:06:09.800
Just like in the comics, he’s also Captain
Singh’s boyfriend.

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:14.619
Although I don’t think Captain Singh knows
anything about him becoming a criminal.

00:06:14.619 --> 00:06:20.610
Episode 11 will probably just tease the character
and then episode 12 will be full blown pied

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:21.610
piper.

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:24.960
One of the more interesting things about him
is that he was born deaf.

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:28.553
The show is changing that, on the show he’ll
be another former Star Labs genius who had

00:06:28.553 --> 00:06:30.050
a falling out with Harrison Wells.

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:31.759
So think Blackout Revenge Episode 7 stuff.

00:06:31.759 --> 00:06:36.249
In this version the particle accelerator explosion
will be the reason he goes deaf.

00:06:36.249 --> 00:06:39.659
As the name implies, his abilities give him
the power of hypnotism.

00:06:39.659 --> 00:06:41.569
One really cool thing about him from the comics
was that he possessed The Anti-Life Equation.

00:06:41.569 --> 00:06:45.039
Which was something Darkseid used to try and
control the minds of every living being.

00:06:45.039 --> 00:06:48.460
It was this mathematical equation that was
supposed to prove the futility of life.

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:57.469
Grant Morrison is the most recent person to
use the idea in a story.

00:06:57.469 --> 00:06:59.240
But they might turn it into an easter egg
on the show.

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:04.449
Most of Grant Morrison’s stuff isn’t accessible
enough for casual viewers so I don’t expect

00:07:04.449 --> 00:07:05.969
them to adapt it.

00:07:05.969 --> 00:07:07.969
But the actual Anti-Life equation is this.

00:07:07.969 --> 00:07:10.659
loneliness + alienation + fear + despair +
self-worth ÷ mockery ÷ condemnation ÷ misunderstanding

00:07:10.659 --> 00:07:13.119
× guilt × shame × failure × judgment n=y
where y=hope and n=folly, love=lies, life=death,

00:07:13.119 --> 00:07:14.119
self=dark side

00:07:14.119 --> 00:07:16.039
Mark Hamill’s character is going to be a
lot of fun.

00:07:16.039 --> 00:07:17.659
He’s playing the classic version of The
Trickster.

00:07:17.659 --> 00:07:22.050
In the comics, the modern incarnation is a
new person who steals all of the Tricksters

00:07:22.050 --> 00:07:23.199
equipment and uses it to start committing
crimes.

00:07:23.199 --> 00:07:24.440
On the show.

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:31.159
Mark Hamill will be a prisoner in Iron Heights
with John Wesley Shipp.

00:07:31.159 --> 00:07:41.020
I hope they get a scene together.

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:52.389
You can view it as a spiritual sequel to his
episode on the classic Flash series.

00:07:52.389 --> 00:07:56.849
So in that timeline he was caught, thrown
in jail and has been there ever since.

00:07:56.849 --> 00:08:06.569
In the new episode, there’s supposed to
be a new person calling themselves the Trickster

00:08:06.569 --> 00:08:08.599
who will be like an imposter.

00:08:08.599 --> 00:08:13.089
And the real Trickster, Mark Hamill, will
help Team Flash take him down.

00:08:13.089 --> 00:08:18.529
Andrew Kriesberg said that he flipped when
he found out Mark Hamill accepted the invitation

00:08:18.529 --> 00:08:22.649
to come on the show.

00:08:22.649 --> 00:08:29.300
Sinceriously, it’s going to be awesome.

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:39.190
That’s pretty much it in terms of Rogues
they’ve already announced on the show.

00:08:39.190 --> 00:08:47.660
Mark Hamill is in Episode 17, so that only
leaves about 3 episodes before the two part

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:48.660
finale.

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:55.680
And they’re probably not going to introduce
new character in the last two episodes.

00:08:55.680 --> 00:09:03.620
If we see any more Rogues it would have to
happen between episode 18 and 20.

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:06.700
Mirror Master would be my next pick.

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:09.900
There have been rumors that Weather Wizard
will come back.

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:14.820
Either his brother will take the mantle or
they’ll twist logic and bring the Clyde

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.980
Martin version back from the dead.

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:21.260
Everyone thinks he’s dead because Joe shot
him at the end of episode 1.

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:28.330
The show mixes and matches villains.

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:34.360
Some of the characters it’s used have been
Firestorm villains, some have been Suicide

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:35.360
Squad members.

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:44.090
We don’t know the titles for the last couple
of episodes, but I think we knew what the

00:09:44.090 --> 00:09:54.710
last couple of Arrow Episode titles were in
season 2 by the end of February.

00:09:54.710 --> 00:09:57.210
Right now they’ve got about 6 more episodes
to film.

00:09:57.210 --> 00:09:58.210
Maybe 7.

00:09:58.210 --> 00:10:01.950
So by the time we see Episode 10, they’ll
probably be shooting Episode 15 or 16.

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:06.460
In related news, I like everyone’s Harrison
Wells theories.

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:21.180
And Yes, I do agree that there are two versions
of The Reverse Flash on the show.

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:29.330
But I don’t think we’ll see the writers
make that clear until the last couple of episodes.

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:35.420
Remember that in the comics, the Hunter Zolomon
Zoom had the Lenses covering his eyes and

00:10:35.420 --> 00:10:38.279
Eobard Thawne didn’t have anything covering
his eyes.

